// DECEMBER 10 — ONE LAST WALK
// December 10 story. Existing scene3.yarn remains available for older playtests.
// The six rooms may be visited in any order. Each memory starts from its named interaction,
// and each memory counts once. An arrival node makes the map exit run Dec10_Memory_RoomExit.
// Room arrival nodes are optional; the six room exits use a quest-specific door node.
// Time advances when leaving after the 2nd, 4th, and 6th completed memories.
// The sixth exit sends Anin directly to the Locker Room at Night.
// Anin's time-change thoughts play on SchoolMap after the transition.
// The rooftop sign, separate Locker Room key sprite, Rooftop Entrance, and
// Rooftop room art are imported. Their scene references must be assigned in Unity.
// Rooftop: Fal leans on the railing (LeanPose, Start Leaning). When Anin walks near,
// the screen fades and she reappears leaning beside Fal before the conversation.
// CAMERA TODO: Pan from rooftop sign to Key Hook, then Janitor's Locker.
// AUDIO: The day_transition cue supplies the time-change bell. No bell rings on the rooftop.
// The Rooftop encounter plays in the Rooftop scene after its entrance notice.

title: Dec10_Declarations
tags: setup testing
---
// Never start this node. These declarations hold progress across room loads.
<<declare $dec10_dressed = false>>
<<declare $dec10_locker_intro_done = false>>
<<declare $dec10_rooftop_checked = false>>
<<declare $dec10_stairway_seen = false>>
<<declare $dec10_missing_key_started = false>>
<<declare $dec10_rooftop_entered = false>>
<<declare $dec10_rooftop_conversation_done = false>>
<<declare $dec10_room_count = 0>>
<<declare $dec10_time_phase = "morning">>
<<declare $dec10_pending_map_thought = "">>
<<declare $dec10_seen_classroom = false>>
<<declare $dec10_seen_photography = false>>
<<declare $dec10_seen_music = false>>
<<declare $dec10_seen_library = false>>
<<declare $dec10_seen_cafetaria = false>>
<<declare $dec10_seen_auditorium = false>>
===

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------
// MORNING — GIRLS' DORM
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------

title: Dec10_Dorm_Morning
tags: december10 dorm morning testing
---
<<cinematic_start>>
// Anin wakes with the existing wake-up animation; Kirana stands by the desk.
// Keep Kirana's opening lines identical when Loop 1 repeats this day.
<<set $dec10_dressed to false>>
<<set $dec10_locker_intro_done to false>>
<<set $dec10_rooftop_checked to false>>
<<set $dec10_stairway_seen to false>>
<<set $dec10_missing_key_started to false>>
<<set $dec10_rooftop_entered to false>>
<<set $dec10_rooftop_conversation_done to false>>
<<set $dec10_room_count to 0>>
<<set $dec10_time_phase to "morning">>
<<set $dec10_pending_map_thought to "">>
<<set $dec10_seen_classroom to false>>
<<set $dec10_seen_photography to false>>
<<set $dec10_seen_music to false>>
<<set $dec10_seen_library to false>>
<<set $dec10_seen_cafetaria to false>>
<<set $dec10_seen_auditorium to false>>
<<set $story_exit to true>>
<<set $anin_dressed to false>>
Kirana: Morning! You ready for our last day?
Anin: Don't remind me.
Kirana: Hey, at least we still have today.
Anin: ...Yeah. We do.
Kirana: I'm heading out. See you at school!
<<close_dialogue_bubble>>
<<door_exit "Kirana" "Dorm">>
// Inner thought. Parentheses distinguish it until a thought presentation exists.
Anin: (Maybe I should take one last walk around school. Before everything changes.)
<<cinematic_end>>
<<quest_start "dec10" "Get ready and go to school">>
// CONTROL ANIN. Desk: Dec10_Dorm_Desk. Door: Dec10_Dorm_Door.
===

title: Dec10_Dorm_Desk
tags: december10 dorm interactable testing
---
<<if $dec10_dressed is false>>
    Anin: I should get dressed.
    -> Get dressed
        <<set $dec10_dressed to true>>
        <<set $anin_dressed to true>>
        <<fade_outfit "Anin" "uniform">>
    -> Cancel
        <<stop>>
<<else>>
    Anin: I'm already wearing my uniform.
<<endif>>
===

title: Dec10_Dorm_Door
tags: december10 dorm interactable testing
---
<<if $dec10_dressed is false>>
    Anin: I can't go out like this.
<<else>>
    <<scene_transition "LockerRoom" "door">>
<<endif>>
===

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------
// LOCKER ROOM — MANDATORY FIRST VISIT
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------

title: Dec10_Lockers_Arrival
tags: december10 lockers testing
---
<<quest_hide_objective "dec10">>
<<if $dec10_room_count >= 6>>
    <<hide "StudentA">>
    <<hide "StudentB">>
<<endif>>
<<if $dec10_room_count >= 6 and $dec10_missing_key_started is false>>
    <<jump Dec10_Lockers_MissingKey>>
<<elseif $dec10_locker_intro_done is false>>
    <<jump Dec10_Lockers_Intro>>
<<endif>>
===

title: Dec10_Lockers_Intro
tags: december10 lockers cutscene testing
---
<<cinematic_start>>
// Two students are already chatting near the lockers.
Student A: You're still not done clearing your locker?
Student B: I just found my first-year ID photo!
Student A: Oh, that haircut...
Student B: Don't. I've suffered enough.
<<close_dialogue_bubble>>
// The screen goes black as the students leave; they are gone when it opens.
<<fade_black_out>>
<<hide "StudentA">>
<<hide "StudentB">>
<<fade_black_in>>
Anin: School. Lively as ever
Anin: Okay. Let's start by getting some fresh air on the rooftop.
<<cinematic_end>>
<<set $dec10_locker_intro_done to true>>
<<quest_update "dec10" "Check the rooftop door">>
// CONTROL ANIN. Both exits refuse to leave until the rooftop door is checked.
===

title: Dec10_Lockers_MapExit
tags: december10 lockers interactable testing
---
<<if $dec10_time_phase == "night" and $dec10_room_count >= 6>>
    Anin: I want to check the rooftop first.
<<elseif $dec10_rooftop_checked is false>>
    Anin: I want to check the rooftop first.
<<else>>
    <<scene_transition "SchoolMap" "door">>
<<endif>>
===

title: Dec10_Lockers_DormExit
tags: december10 lockers interactable testing
---
<<if $dec10_time_phase == "night" and $dec10_room_count >= 6>>
    Anin: I want to check the rooftop first.
<<elseif $dec10_rooftop_checked is false>>
    Anin: I want to check the rooftop first.
<<else>>
    Anin: It's our last day at school. I'm not spending it in the dorm.
<<endif>>
===

title: Dec10_KeyHook
tags: december10 lockers interactable testing
---
<<if $dec10_missing_key_started is false>>
    // The janitor's locker key is still hanging here.
    <<face_character "Anin" "left">>
    Anin: (I think that is the key to the Janitor's Locker.)
<<else>>
    // The separate key sprite hides when $dec10_missing_key_started becomes true.
    Anin: (The janitor's locker key is missing.)
<<endif>>
===

title: Dec10_JanitorLocker
tags: december10 lockers interactable testing
---
// The locker is still locked in the morning. Fal takes the key before Anin returns at night.
Anin: (It's locked. I'm not touching that.)
===

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------
// SIX ROOM MEMORIES — START ON FIRST ROOM ENTRY, IN ANY ORDER
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------

// Configure one YarnCutscene per room to start its Dec10_*_Arrival node.
// The arrival node runs on every entry; the memory and walk run only once.
title: Dec10_Classroom_Arrival
tags: december10 classroom testing
---
<<set $story_exit to true>>
<<jump Dec10_Memory_Classroom>>
===

title: Dec10_Photography_Arrival
tags: december10 photographyclub testing
---
<<set $story_exit to true>>
<<jump Dec10_Memory_Photography>>
===

title: Dec10_Music_Arrival
tags: december10 musicroom testing
---
<<set $story_exit to true>>
<<jump Dec10_Memory_Music>>
===

title: Dec10_Library_Arrival
tags: december10 library testing
---
<<set $story_exit to true>>
<<jump Dec10_Memory_Library>>
===

title: Dec10_Cafetaria_Arrival
tags: december10 cafetaria testing
---
<<set $story_exit to true>>
<<jump Dec10_Memory_Cafetaria>>
===

title: Dec10_Auditorium_Arrival
tags: december10 auditorium testing
---
<<set $story_exit to true>>
<<jump Dec10_Memory_Auditorium>>
===

title: Dec10_Memory_Classroom
tags: december10 classroom memory interactable testing
---
// First entry: Anin walks to her old desk before remembering it.
<<if $dec10_locker_intro_done is true and $dec10_seen_classroom is false>>
    <<place_character_near_x "Anin" 5.84 8>>
    <<start_character_move "Anin" 5.84 4 "walk" 0>>
    <<cinematic_start>>
    <<wait_for_character_moves>>
    <<face_character "Anin" "right">>
    Anin: (I used to sit here so nobody would notice me leaving.)
    Anin: (Now there's always someone waiting for me.)
    <<cinematic_end>>
    <<set $dec10_seen_classroom to true>>
    <<set $dec10_room_count to $dec10_room_count + 1>>
<<endif>>
===

title: Dec10_Classroom_AninDesk
tags: scene10 classroom interactable
---
Anin: Good old desk. I'll miss you after graduation... or not.
===

title: Dec10_Memory_Photography
tags: december10 photographyclub memory interactable testing
---
// First entry: Anin approaches Lila, who turns to face her.
<<if $dec10_locker_intro_done is true and $dec10_seen_photography is false>>
    <<place_character_near_actor "Anin" "LilaSceneDec10" 2.5 8>>
    <<start_character_move_to_actor "Anin" "LilaSceneDec10" 2.5 4 "walk" 0>>
    <<cinematic_start>>
    <<wait_for_character_moves>>
    <<face_character_to_actor "LilaSceneDec10" "Anin">>
    Lila: Anin! Look what I found while sorting photos for my interview!
    Anin: Please tell me I don't look awkward.
    Lila: Worse. You're actually smiling!
    Anin: ...Really?
    Lila: You were laughing so hard you forgot to hide from my camera.
    Anin: You kept that?
    Lila: Obviously. Don't make it weird.
    <<cinematic_end>>
    <<set $dec10_seen_photography to true>>
    <<set $dec10_room_count to $dec10_room_count + 1>>
<<endif>>
===

title: Dec10_Memory_Music
tags: december10 musicroom memory interactable testing
---
// First entry: Anin walks toward the microphone or music stand.
<<if $dec10_locker_intro_done is true and $dec10_seen_music is false>>
    <<place_character_near_x "Anin" 11.6 8>>
    <<start_character_move "Anin" 11.6 4 "walk" 0>>
    <<cinematic_start>>
    <<wait_for_character_moves>>
    Anin: (Lila made me sing here once. I was terrified.)
    Anin: (Then everyone joined in. Somehow, they were even worse.)
    <<cinematic_end>>
    <<set $dec10_seen_music to true>>
    <<set $dec10_room_count to $dec10_room_count + 1>>
<<endif>>
===

title: Dec10_Music_Instrument
tags: scene10 classroom interactable
---
Anin: I would love to someday be able to play one of this things
===

title: Dec10_Memory_Library
tags: december10 library memory interactable testing
---
// First entry: Anin approaches her old reading spot.
<<if $dec10_locker_intro_done is true and $dec10_seen_library is false>>
    <<place_character_near_x "Anin" -1.26 8>>
    <<start_character_move "Anin" -1.26 4 "walk" 0>>
    <<cinematic_start>>
    <<wait_for_character_moves>>
    Anin: (Dira found me hiding here during lunch.)
    Anin: (She didn't ask me to talk. She just stayed.)
    <<cinematic_end>>
    <<set $dec10_seen_library to true>>
    <<set $dec10_room_count to $dec10_room_count + 1>>
<<endif>>
===

title: Dec10_Memory_Cafetaria
tags: december10 cafetaria memory interactable testing
---
// First entry: Anin approaches Kirana at their usual table. She is seated and has already ordered.
<<if $dec10_locker_intro_done is true and $dec10_seen_cafetaria is false>>
    <<place_character_near_actor "Anin" "KiranaSceneDec10" -2.5 8>>
    <<start_character_move_to_actor "Anin" "KiranaSceneDec10" -2.5 4 "walk" 0>>
    <<cinematic_start>>
    <<wait_for_character_moves>>
    Kirana: Hey! Same table! I already ordered for us.
    Anin: One last lunch here, huh?
    Kirana: When I move, I'll find us a table just like this.
    Anin: But we won't get to eat together every day.
    Kirana: No. But I'll save you a seat whenever you visit.
    Anin: ...Promise?
    Kirana: Obviously!
    <<cinematic_end>>
    <<set $dec10_seen_cafetaria to true>>
    <<set $dec10_room_count to $dec10_room_count + 1>>
<<endif>>
===

title: Dec10_Memory_Auditorium
tags: december10 auditorium memory interactable testing
---
// First entry: Anin approaches Dira, who turns right to face her.
<<if $dec10_locker_intro_done is true and $dec10_seen_auditorium is false>>
    <<place_character_near_actor "Anin" "DiraSceneDec10" 2.5 8>>
    <<start_character_move_to_actor "Anin" "DiraSceneDec10" 2.5 4 "walk" 0>>
    <<cinematic_start>>
    <<wait_for_character_moves>>
    <<face_character "DiraSceneDec10" "right">>
    Anin: Still checking everything?
    Dira: Two names were missing from the seating chart. Fixed it.
    Anin: You really have everything figured out. Even university.
    Dira: I've submitted my applications. That's the easy part.
    Anin: There's a hard part?
    Dira: Not knowing what it'll actually be like.
    Anin: ...You're worried too?
    Dira: A little. I can make plans, Anin. I can't predict everything.
    <<cinematic_end>>
    <<set $dec10_seen_auditorium to true>>
    <<set $dec10_room_count to $dec10_room_count + 1>>
<<endif>>
===

// Each memory room's map exit runs this node. Entering alone does not increase the count;
// only completing a memory interaction does. The time transition runs here,
// then Dec10_Map_Arrival speaks after the SchoolMap opens.
title: Dec10_Memory_RoomExit
tags: december10 memory exit testing
---
<<if $dec10_room_count == 2 and $dec10_time_phase == "morning">>
    <<set $dec10_time_phase to "lunch">>
    <<set $dec10_pending_map_thought to "lunch">>
    <<advance_time_to_scene "lunch" "SchoolMap">>
<<elseif $dec10_room_count == 4 and $dec10_time_phase == "lunch">>
    <<set $dec10_time_phase to "after_school">>
    <<set $dec10_pending_map_thought to "after_school">>
    <<advance_time_to_scene "after_school" "SchoolMap">>
<<elseif $dec10_room_count == 6 and $dec10_time_phase == "after_school">>
    <<set $dec10_time_phase to "night">>
    // The time transition supplies the bell; the Locker Room's SchoolMap door supplies the spawn and facing.
    <<advance_time_to_scene_at_door "night" "LockerRoom" "SchoolMap">>
<<else>>
    <<scene_transition "SchoolMap">>
<<endif>>
===

// Run on every SchoolMap arrival during December 10. A pending thought exists
// only after the second or fourth memory room's time transition.
title: Dec10_Map_Arrival
tags: december10 schoolmap testing
---
<<wait_for_time_transition>>
<<if $dec10_pending_map_thought == "lunch">>
    <<set $dec10_pending_map_thought to "">>
    <<dialogue_bottom_left true>>
    Anin: (Already lunchtime? Guess the cafeteria will be packed right around now.)
    <<close_dialogue_bubble>>
    <<dialogue_bottom_left false>>
<<elseif $dec10_pending_map_thought == "after_school">>
    <<set $dec10_pending_map_thought to "">>
    <<dialogue_bottom_left true>>
    Anin: (Time is setting already, I need to pick up the pace.)
    <<close_dialogue_bubble>>
    <<dialogue_bottom_left false>>
<<endif>>
===

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------
// NIGHT — THE MISSING KEY AND FAL
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------

title: Dec10_Lockers_MissingKey
tags: december10 lockers night cutscene testing
---
<<cinematic_start>>
<<set $dec10_missing_key_started to true>>
// The incoming time transition fades to black and rings the school bell once.
// The separate key sprite hides here when the variable changes.
// Anin enters beside the SchoolMap door; the students are gone.
Anin: (I think that's everywhere...)
Anin: But it's weird though, i didn't see Fal anywhere today
Anin: Wait, the Key Hook, it's empty
Anin: I smell a case here
<<cinematic_end>>
<<quest_update "dec10" "Go to the rooftop">>
// CONTROL ANIN. Fal has already used the key; no locker interaction is required.
===

title: Dec10_RooftopDoor
tags: december10 lockers rooftop interactable testing
---
<<if $dec10_time_phase == "night" and $dec10_room_count >= 6>>
    <<jump Dec10_Rooftop_Enter>>
<<elseif $dec10_rooftop_checked is false>>
    // <<cinematic_start>>
    Anin: Ah. The door is locked
    <<story_splash "rooftop_sign">>
    Anin: (Aw, I wanted to see the view one last time.)
    <<story_splash_end>>
    // CAMERA TODO: Pan to the Key Hook, then the Janitor's Locker.
    <<face_character "Anin" "left">>
    Anin: (I think that is the key to the Janitor's Locker.)
    Anin: (The rooftop key's probably in there.)
    Anin: (...Yeah, I'm not touching that.)
    Anin: (Guess I'll look around the school first.)
    // <<cinematic_end>>
    <<set $dec10_rooftop_checked to true>>
    <<quest_update "dec10" "Explore the school">>
<<else>>
    Anin: Ah. The door is locked
<<endif>>
===

title: Dec10_Stairway
tags: december10 stairway cutscene testing
---
// Start this node on first arrival in the Rooftop Entrance scene.
<<if $dec10_stairway_seen is false>>
    <<cinematic_start>>
    // Anin sees the notice beside the unlocked rooftop door.
    <<detour Dec10_Rooftop_Notice>>
    <<cinematic_end>>
    <<set $dec10_stairway_seen to true>>
    <<quest_update "dec10" "Enter the rooftop">>
<<endif>>
// CONTROL ANIN. Use this room's door to enter the Rooftop scene.
===

title: Dec10_Rooftop_Notice
tags: december10 stairway interactable testing
---
NO ENTRY AFTER 6 PM.
===

title: Dec10_Rooftop_Enter
tags: december10 rooftop door interactable testing
---
<<if $dec10_time_phase == "night" and $dec10_room_count >= 6>>
    // Enter the stairway room. Its arrival node shows the rooftop notice.
    <<scene_transition "Rooftop Entrance" "door">>
<<endif>>
===

title: Dec10_Rooftop_Encounter
tags: december10 rooftop cutscene testing
---
<<cinematic_start>>
// Anin unexpectedly finds Fal by the railing, looking out over the school.
// Fal is already leaning (LeanPose with Start Leaning in the Rooftop scene).
// The screen fades; Anin reappears leaning on Fal's left. Tune the X offset to the art:
// -1.6875 = 27 px left of Fal's root (25 px wide Anin sprite + 2 px gap).
<<set $dec10_rooftop_entered to true>>
<<fade_teleport_character_to_actor "Anin" "Fal" -1.6875 "lean">>
Anin: Fal? Didn't expect to see you here.
Fal: Just needed somewhere quiet.
<<jump Dec10_Rooftop_Conversation>>
===

title: Dec10_Rooftop_Conversation
tags: december10 rooftop cutscene testing
---
Anin: You always seem like you've got everything figured out.
Fal: I know I want to study aerospace. Getting my parents to agree? That's another story.
Anin: Really? I thought you'd know how to convince them.
Fal: So did I.
Anin: ...Guess even you don't have all the answers.
Fal: Not even close.
Anin: Want me to change the subject?
Fal: Nah. It's nice talking to someone who listens.
Anin: ...I can do that.
Fal: I know. That's why I like talking to you.
<<close_dialogue_bubble>>
// A brief, comfortable silence.
<<delay 0.7>>
Anin: We should probably head down.
Fal: Yeah.
Fal: ...I'm glad you came up here.
Anin: Me too.
// Fade again: Anin steps off the railing and stands beside Fal, facing him. Fal keeps leaning.
// Facing set while leaning is kept for when she stands. -0.375 = 6 px left of Fal's root,
// which leaves ~15 px between standing Anin and leaning Fal (his Lean Offset X is 1.9).
<<face_character_to_actor "Anin" "Fal">>
<<fade_teleport_character_to_actor "Anin" "Fal" -0.375 "stand">>
// Goodbye side by side, before Anin walks to the exit door.
Fal: I'll see you tomorrow, Anin.
Anin: Yeah. See you tomorrow.
<<cinematic_end>>
<<quest_update "dec10" "Leave the rooftop">>
<<set $dec10_rooftop_conversation_done to true>>
// CONTROL ANIN. Rooftop exit interaction: Dec10_Rooftop_Exit.
===

title: Dec10_Rooftop_Exit
tags: december10 rooftop exit testing
---
<<if $dec10_rooftop_conversation_done is false>>
    Anin: I should talk to Fal first.
    <<stop>>
<<endif>>
// Anin already said goodbye beside Fal at the end of Dec10_Rooftop_Conversation.
// Fal stays at the railing. Anin walks back toward the Dorm through the quiet school.
<<cinematic_start>>
// HIDDEN CONTEXT: Fal is already experiencing a serious mental health crisis.
// Anin does not recognize it. This connection is meaningful but does not resolve it.
Anin: (I thought Fal had everything figured out.)
Anin: (Guess we're all a little scared of tomorrow.)
Anin: (I'm going to miss this.)
<<cinematic_end>>
<<scene_transition "Dorm">>
===

title: Dec10_Dorm_Return
tags: december10 dorm night testing
---
<<if $dec10_wish_resume is true>>
    <<set $dec10_wish_resume to false>>
    <<jump Dec10_Wish_AfterFlashback>>
<<endif>>
// Anin returns alone. Continue directly into the wish cutscene.
<<hide "Kirana">>
<<quest_clear>>
<<jump Dec10_Wish_Dorm>>
===
